{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/RemoteChange","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"RemoteChange","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every field describes the whole burst, not its last notification. A burst is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one window as far as the merge is concerned, and “the last one wins” would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"silently drop every notification but one — on a debounce that exists"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"precisely because bursts are expected, that is a change quietly going"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"missing rather than a visible failure."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only notifications the observer "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"accepted"}]},{"type":"text","text":" are represented. A notification"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from a store the observer was told it doesn’t own is dropped before it gets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"here; one whose store can’t be identified is always accepted, and sets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/RemoteChange\/includesUnidentifiedStore"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Why there is no history token","type":"heading","anchor":"Why-there-is-no-history-token"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The underlying notification carries "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPersistentHistoryTokenKey"},{"type":"text","text":", and it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deliberately not surfaced. That value is a CoreData "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPersistentHistoryToken"},{"type":"text","text":";"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the watermark in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" is a SwiftData "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DefaultHistoryToken"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose only public initializer is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":" — there is no supported"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conversion between the two, and SwiftData’s interface names no CoreData type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at all. Publishing a token that neither Swidux nor an app author can act on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"would be an invitation to misuse it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"PersistenceCoordinator.mergeChanges(into:policy:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" anchors its watermark on the last transaction in the window it just scanned, so it already holds the token it needs."}]}]}],"metadata":{"title":"RemoteChange","roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RemoteChange","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"SwiduxCloudKitSync"}],"externalID":"s:18SwiduxCloudKitSync12RemoteChangeV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RemoteChange","kind":"identifier"}]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The stores one coalesced burst of remote-chang